installing Micronix 1.67 on a simulated hard disk
=================================================

	./run

which opens an xterm for the console and boots the 1.67 standalone
floppy off the simulated DJ/DMA.  The window this is started from stays
the simulator's own monitor, and system calls scroll past in it as they
happen - which is the reason for putting the console in a window of its
own.  Each line names the task and the address the call came from, so

	tsk1:43f3 micronix stat("/dev/ttyA", f7db

can be handed straight back to the simulator as -T tsk1:43f3 to start an
instruction trace there.  If the calls are more than you want, take
-t 0x80000 out of run.

Wait for the welcome.  It takes a few minutes of simulated time to get
from the loader to a shell - the banner appears early and then nothing
happens for a while, which is normal - and the shell gives no prompt, so
the last line you see is

	Then boot Micronix from the hard disk. If you have any
	questions, please read the Installation section of the
	Micronix User's Manual.

Anything typed before that point is thrown away when the shell sets up
the terminal, which is worth knowing because it looks like the machine
ignoring you.  When it has settled, type

	source m5init

and it will mkfs /dev/m5a, fsck it, mount it on /b, copy the running
system across with cptree, relink /b/dev/root and /b/dev/swap, patch the
kernel's root and swap devices with ddt, tidy up and unmount.  It prints
"Disk initialization complete." when it is done.  cptree is copying a
whole filesystem through a simulated Z80, so give it time.

what is here
------------

    standalone167.bin	the 1.67 standalone, with one byte changed
    sa67.5.skew.1k	the name that gives it its geometry, via bdev(2,93)
    hddma-0		the drive to install on, blank, 5 meg
    hddma-1		a second drive, blank, for swap

The one changed byte is the swap device.  Micronix ships with

	root dev: djdma/76
	swap dev: nodev/0

and with no swap device it prints "No more space on disk nodev/0" and
gets no further than the banner - balloc failing on device zero.  The
swap word is the second of the two device words in the kernel image, the
pair that m5init itself patches with "ddt /b/micronix sB6CB 0 3 0 3", and
here it points at hddma/1 so the install has drive 0 to itself.

Why it needs to swap at all is not understood - the disk shipped without
a swap device, so the real machine did not need one - so treat that byte
as a workaround rather than a fix.  See hwsim/DISKS.

afterwards
----------

m5init does not write a boot block, and nothing else does either: the rom
reads cylinder 0 head 0 sector 0 of the hard disk and there is nothing
there.  See hwsim/DISKS for what that takes - micronix/stand builds the
two levels and cmd/installboot puts them in a file that owns cylinder 0,
which is what keeps the filesystem from allocating over them.

Use 1.67 and not 1.6.  1.6's kernel has its root device as djdma/12,
which is the single sided minor for a disk that is double sided, and it
stops in the rom monitor before reaching a shell.  1.67 has 76.
